  "body": "**The request (the maintainer, relayed 2026-11-17):** \"have it setup a bunch of examples.. for debugging..\" - \"a good way of testing the various operations\", with the screenshots on a separate images branch, docs off the operation pages, and maybe PDFs and CamCraft projects \"with stuff pre done\", e.g. \"Setup a basic spun profile turning operation having a conical shape with a threaded end\".\n\n## What\n\nA catalog of small, real use cases, one folder each, built from source (never hand-saved):\n\n- `examples/catalog/<family>/<case>/`: the model and its generator script (original geometry), the `.camproj` built headlessly by a committed script (script verbs / MCP, the same undoable commands the GUI uses), the posted program for the case's machine, and a short README (what it shows, the steps, what to look at).\n- One test per case: open the project, regenerate, verify clean (no gouge, no refusal unless the case is about a refusal), and compare the posted program with the committed one. So every example is also a regression fixture.\n- Screenshots rendered reproducibly (#1902's off-screen pipeline) onto an images-only branch, linked from the docs; optional PDF per case (pandoc + headless Chrome, as the tutorial build does).\n- Docs: each operation page links its cases.\n\n## Families (one sub-issue per case, filed as they are built)\n\nTurning (profile, groove, thread, face, part-off), 2D (face, pocket, contour, adaptive, drill pattern, chamfer/deburr), 3D (adaptive roughing, parallel/waterline finish, rest), multi-axis (3+1 indexed - after #2389, wrapped A, 3+2), wire/sinker EDM, plasma/laser, probing.\n\nSub-issues: the catalog infrastructure first, then cases. Bugs found while building a case are filed on their own and linked here.\n",
